IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa4-notification.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10, Chapter 1: "Notification of information about
-- directors" (ss 167G to 167N) and "Directors: duties relating to ID verification and notification", lines 2182-2281
-- of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- SOURCE and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa4-requirements.l4. Every branch carries its FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment.
-- Two decisions made once for this module (NOTES.md, forks F5 and F19):
--   * a question "does the notice contain what paragraph (x) requires?" answers NOTHING where the paragraph's own "if" or
--     "where" is unmet (the paragraph says nothing of that notice); a question "is the company obliged to ...?" answers
--     JUST FALSE where the condition is unmet.
--   * a period "of 14 days beginning with the day on which X": the first day is the day of X, so the last day is
--     X plus 13 days; as a regulative rule the clock starts at 0 on the day of X and the duty is WITHIN 13.
-- Naming: every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.

-- ---- s 167G: duty to notify registrar of change in directors --------------------------------------------------

-- (1) with (5): the duty arises when a person becomes or ceases to be a director; on incorporation it does not arise for a
-- person named as a proposed director in the statement under section 12.
-- src:2183 | 167G Duty to notify registrar of change in directors
-- src:2184 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person—
-- src:2185 | (a) becomes a director of the company, or
-- src:2186 | (b) ceases to be a director of the company.
-- src:2202 | (5) Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as a proposed director in the statement under section 12.
@ref s 167G(1) and (5) Duty to notify registrar of change in directors (src:2183-2186 and src:2202)
GIVEN `a person becomes a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person ceases to be a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person became a director on the company's incorporation and is named as a proposed director in the statement under section 12` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(1) the company is obliged to give notice to the registrar of the change` MEANS
    IF `the person became a director on the company's incorporation and is named as a proposed director in the statement under section 12`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1)(a) does not require a company, on its incorporation, to give notice in relation to a person named as a proposed director in the statement under section 12."
    ELSE IF `a person becomes a director of the company` OR `a person ceases to be a director of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar if a person— (a) becomes a director of the company, or (b) ceases to be a director of the company."

-- src:2187 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be a director of the company.
@ref s 167G(2) The notice must specify the date (src:2187)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the person became or ceased to be a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(2) the notice specifies the date as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the date on which the person became or ceased to be a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must specify the date on which the person became or ceased to be a director of the company."

-- (3): what a notice of a person having become a director must contain. The facts about the notice and the person
-- are one record, so that the six paragraphs can be separate functions over it.
-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2189 | (a) a statement of the required information about the new director (see sections 167J and 167K);
-- src:2190 | (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity;
-- src:2191 | (c) if the person is an individual, a statement that their identity is verified (see section 1110A);
-- src:2192 | (d) a statement that the person is not—
-- src:2193 | (i) disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)), or
-- src:2194 | (ii) otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment for appointment as a director;
-- src:2195 | (e) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation but for the permission of a court to act, a statement to that effect specifying—
-- src:2196 | (i) the court by which permission was given, and
-- src:2197 | (ii) the date on which permission was given.
-- src:2198 | (f) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (designated persons under sanctions legislation) but for the authority of a licence of the kind mentioned in that section or Article, a statement to that effect specifying—
-- src:2199 | (i) the date on which the licence was issued, and
-- src:2200 | (ii) by whom it was issued.
@ref s 167G(3) The notice of a person having become a director (src:2188-2200)
DECLARE `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director` HAS
    `the notice contains a statement of the required information about the new director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement that the person's identity is verified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement that the person is not disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement that the person is not otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment for appointment as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation but for the permission of a court to act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying the court by which permission was given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying the date on which permission was given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person would be disqualified by virtue of section 11A of the 1986 Act or Article 15A of the 2002 Order but for the authority of a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying the date on which the licence was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying by whom the licence was issued` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2189 | (a) a statement of the required information about the new director (see sections 167J and 167K);
@ref s 167G(3)(a) A statement of the required information (src:2188-2189)
GIVEN n IS A `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(3)(a) the notice contains a statement of the required information about the new director` MEANS
    IF n's `the notice contains a statement of the required information about the new director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain— (a) a statement of the required information about the new director (see sections 167J and 167K)"

-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2189 | (a) a statement of the required information about the new director (see sections 167J and 167K);
-- src:2190 | (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity;
@ref s 167G(3)(b) A statement that the person has consented to act (src:2188-2190)
GIVEN n IS A `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(3)(b) the notice contains a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity` MEANS
    IF n's `the notice contains a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity"

-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2191 | (c) if the person is an individual, a statement that their identity is verified (see section 1110A);
@ref s 167G(3)(c) A statement that the identity of an individual is verified (src:2188 and src:2191)
GIVEN n IS A `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(3)(c) the notice contains a statement that the individual's identity is verified` MEANS
    IF NOT (n's `the person is an individual`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) if the person is an individual, a statement that their identity is verified (see section 1110A)"; the paragraph says nothing of a person who is not an individual
    ELSE IF n's `the notice contains a statement that the person's identity is verified`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person is an individual, a statement that their identity is verified"

-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2192 | (d) a statement that the person is not—
-- src:2193 | (i) disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)), or
-- src:2194 | (ii) otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment for appointment as a director;
@ref s 167G(3)(d) A statement that the person is not disqualified or otherwise ineligible (src:2188 and src:2192-2194)
GIVEN n IS A `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(3)(d) the notice contains a statement that the person is neither disqualified nor otherwise ineligible` MEANS
    IF       n's `the notice contains a statement that the person is not disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation`
         AND n's `the notice contains a statement that the person is not otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment for appointment as a director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) a statement that the person is not— (i) disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)), or (ii) otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment for appointment as a director"

-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2195 | (e) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation but for the permission of a court to act, a statement to that effect specifying—
-- src:2196 | (i) the court by which permission was given, and
-- src:2197 | (ii) the date on which permission was given.
@ref s 167G(3)(e) A statement where the person is disqualified but for the permission of a court (src:2188 and src:2195-2197)
GIVEN n IS A `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(3)(e) the notice contains a statement of the court and the date of the permission` MEANS
    IF NOT (n's `the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation but for the permission of a court to act`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation but for the permission of a court to act"; the paragraph says nothing of another person
    ELSE IF       n's `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying the court by which permission was given`
              AND n's `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying the date on which permission was given`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement to that effect specifying— (i) the court by which permission was given, and (ii) the date on which permission was given"

-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2198 | (f) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (designated persons under sanctions legislation) but for the authority of a licence of the kind mentioned in that section or Article, a statement to that effect specifying—
-- src:2199 | (i) the date on which the licence was issued, and
-- src:2200 | (ii) by whom it was issued.
@ref s 167G(3)(f) A statement where the person is disqualified but for the authority of a licence (src:2188 and src:2198-2200)
GIVEN n IS A `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(3)(f) the notice contains a statement of the date and issuer of the licence` MEANS
    IF NOT (n's `the person would be disqualified by virtue of section 11A of the 1986 Act or Article 15A of the 2002 Order but for the authority of a licence`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(f) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (designated persons under sanctions legislation) but for the authority of a licence"; the paragraph says nothing of another person
    ELSE IF       n's `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying the date on which the licence was issued`
              AND n's `the notice contains a statement to that effect specifying by whom the licence was issued`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement to that effect specifying— (i) the date on which the licence was issued, and (ii) by whom it was issued"

-- (3) as a whole: every paragraph that applies to the notice is met. A paragraph answering NOTHING does not apply to this
-- notice (its own "if" is unmet) and is skipped; one JUST FALSE makes the notice fall short (fork F19).
-- src:2188 | (3) A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain—
-- src:2189 | (a) a statement of the required information about the new director (see sections 167J and 167K);
-- src:2190 | (b) a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity;
-- src:2191 | (c) if the person is an individual, a statement that their identity is verified (see section 1110A);
-- src:2192 | (d) a statement that the person is not—
-- src:2193 | (i) disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see section 159A(2)), or
-- src:2194 | (ii) otherwise ineligible by virtue of any enactment for appointment as a director;
-- src:2195 | (e) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation but for the permission of a court to act, a statement to that effect specifying—
-- src:2196 | (i) the court by which permission was given, and
-- src:2197 | (ii) the date on which permission was given.
-- src:2198 | (f) if the person would be disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation by virtue of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 or Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (designated persons under sanctions legislation) but for the authority of a licence of the kind mentioned in that section or Article, a statement to that effect specifying—
-- src:2199 | (i) the date on which the licence was issued, and
-- src:2200 | (ii) by whom it was issued.
@ref s 167G(3) The notice of a person having become a director must contain (src:2188-2200)
GIVEN n IS A `s 167G(3) the notice of a person having become a director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(3) the notice contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST FALSE)
           (LIST `s 167G(3)(a) the notice contains a statement of the required information about the new director` n
               , `s 167G(3)(b) the notice contains a statement by the company that the person has consented to act in that capacity` n
               , `s 167G(3)(c) the notice contains a statement that the individual's identity is verified` n
               , `s 167G(3)(d) the notice contains a statement that the person is neither disqualified nor otherwise ineligible` n
               , `s 167G(3)(e) the notice contains a statement of the court and the date of the permission` n
               , `s 167G(3)(f) the notice contains a statement of the date and issuer of the licence` n)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1)(a) of a person having become a director must contain"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4): "permission of a court to act" means permission of a court under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table
-- in section 159A(2).
-- src:2201 | (4) In subsection (3)(e) “permission of a court to act” means permission of a court under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2).
@ref s 167G(4) Permission of a court to act (src:2201)
GIVEN `the permission is permission of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permission is given under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(4) the permission is permission of a court to act` MEANS
    IF `the permission is permission of a court` AND `the permission is given under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“permission of a court to act” means permission of a court under a provision mentioned in column 2 of the table in section 159A(2)"

-- (6): "within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be a director".
-- src:2203 | (6) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be a director.
@ref s 167G(6) The last day for giving the notice (src:2203)
GIVEN `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 167G(6) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` MEANS
    `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` PLUS 13

-- src:2203 | (6) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be a director.
@ref s 167G(6) The notice must be given within the period (src:2203)
GIVEN `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167G(6) the notice is given within the period of 14 days` MEANS
    IF       `the day the notice is given` AT LEAST `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director`
         AND `the day the notice is given` AT MOST (`s 167G(6) the last day of the period of 14 days beginning with the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director` `the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be a director."

-- s 167G(1) and (6) as a regulative rule: the clock starts at 0 on the day the person becomes or ceases to be a director,
-- and the 14th day is clock 13 (the period "beginning with the day").
-- src:2183 | 167G Duty to notify registrar of change in directors
-- src:2184 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person—
-- src:2185 | (a) becomes a director of the company, or
-- src:2186 | (b) ceases to be a director of the company.
-- src:2203 | (6) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the person becomes or ceases to be a director.
@ref s 167G(1) and (6) The company's duty to notify the registrar (regulative rule) (src:2183-2186 and src:2203)
`s 167G(1) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar of the change in directors` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the change in directors under section 167G"
    WITHIN 13
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "notice of the change in directors was not given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the person became or ceased to be a director"

-- ---- s 167H: duty to notify registrar of changes of information -------------------------------------------------

-- src:2205 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a director (see sections 167J and 167K).
@ref s 167H(1) Duty to notify registrar of changes of information (src:2205)
GIVEN `the required information about a director has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167H(1) the company is obliged to give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` MEANS
    IF `the required information about a director has changed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a director"

-- src:2206 | (2) The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred.
@ref s 167H(2) The notice must specify the date of the change (src:2206)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167H(2) the notice specifies the date of the change as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must specify the date on which the change occurred."

-- src:2207 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 167H(3) The notice must be given within the period (src:2207)
GIVEN `the day the change occurs` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167H(3) the notice is given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the change occurs` MEANS
    IF       `the day the notice is given` AT LEAST `the day the change occurs`
         AND `the day the notice is given` AT MOST (`the day the change occurs` PLUS 13)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs."

-- src:2205 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a director (see sections 167J and 167K).
-- src:2207 | (3) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the change occurs.
@ref s 167H(1) and (3) The company's duty to notify the registrar of a change of information (regulative rule) (src:2205 and src:2207)
`s 167H(1) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar of the change in the required information` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the change in the required information under section 167H"
    WITHIN 13
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "notice of the change was not given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the change occurred"

-- (4): where a service address changes but not the residential address, the notice must say the residential address is unchanged.
-- src:2208 | (4) Where a company gives notice of a change of a director’s service address but not their residential address, the notice must contain a statement that the residential address is unchanged.
@ref s 167H(4) A change of service address but not residential address (src:2208)
GIVEN `the notice is of a change of a director's service address but not their residential address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice contains a statement that the residential address is unchanged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167H(4) the notice contains the statement that the residential address is unchanged as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the notice is of a change of a director's service address but not their residential address`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company gives notice of a change of a director’s service address but not their residential address"; the subsection says nothing of another notice (fork F5)
    ELSE IF `the notice contains a statement that the residential address is unchanged`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice must contain a statement that the residential address is unchanged"

-- ---- s 167I: notification of changes occurring before company's incorporation ------------------------------------

-- src:2210 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person named in the statement under section 12 as a proposed director of the company did not become a director on its incorporation.
@ref s 167I(1) A proposed director who did not become a director on incorporation (src:2210)
GIVEN `a person named in the statement under section 12 as a proposed director of the company did not become a director on its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167I(1) the company is obliged to give notice to the registrar that the proposed director did not become a director` MEANS
    IF `a person named in the statement under section 12 as a proposed director of the company did not become a director on its incorporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar if a person named in the statement under section 12 as a proposed director of the company did not become a director on its incorporation."

-- src:2211 | (2) A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a proposed director that occurred—
-- src:2212 | (a) after the application for the company’s registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar, but
-- src:2213 | (b) before the company was incorporated.
