    IF       `the required information about a proposed director changed after the application for the company's registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar`
         AND `the change occurred before the company was incorporated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must give notice to the registrar of any change in the required information about a proposed director that occurred— (a) after the application for the company’s registration under section 9 was delivered to the registrar, but (b) before the company was incorporated."

-- (3): not required under (2) in respect of a person if the company gives notice under (1) in respect of the person.
-- src:2214 | (3) But a company is not required to give notice under subsection (2) in respect of a person if it gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person.
@ref s 167I(3) No notice under subsection (2) where notice is given under subsection (1) (src:2214)
GIVEN `the company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167I(3) the company is required to give notice under subsection (2) in respect of the person` MEANS
    IF `the company gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But a company is not required to give notice under subsection (2) in respect of a person if it gives notice under subsection (1) in respect of the person."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only what happens if notice is given under subsection (1); whether notice is otherwise required is subsection (2)

-- src:2215 | (4) A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date on which the change occurred.
@ref s 167I(4) A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date (src:2215)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167I(4) the notice specifies the date of the change as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the date on which the change occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (2) must specify the date on which the change occurred."

-- src:2216 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 167I(5) The notice must be given within the period (src:2216)
GIVEN `the day the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167I(5) the notice is given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the company was incorporated` MEANS
    IF       `the day the notice is given` AT LEAST `the day the company was incorporated`
         AND `the day the notice is given` AT MOST (`the day the company was incorporated` PLUS 13)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated."

-- src:2210 | (1) A company must give notice to the registrar if a person named in the statement under section 12 as a proposed director of the company did not become a director on its incorporation.
-- src:2216 | (5) A notice under this section must be given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day on which the company was incorporated.
@ref s 167I(1), (2) and (5) The company's duties before incorporation (regulative rule) (src:2210 and src:2216)
`s 167I(5) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar of the matters before incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "give notice of the matters under section 167I"
    WITHIN 13
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "notice under section 167I was not given within the period of 14 days beginning with the day the company was incorporated"

-- ---- s 167J: required information about a director: individuals ------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 167J(1) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 167J(1)(a) name, date of birth and nationality`
    `s 167J(1)(b) any relevant former names`
    `s 167J(1)(c) a service address`
    `s 167J(1)(d) usual residential address`
    `s 167J(1)(e) the part of the United Kingdom, or the country or state outside it, in which the individual is usually resident`
    `s 167J(1) any other information`

-- src:2217 | 167J Required information about a director: individuals
-- src:2218 | (1) The required information about a director (or proposed director) who is an individual is—
-- src:2219 | (a) name, date of birth and nationality;
-- src:2220 | (b) any relevant former names;
-- src:2221 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”);
-- src:2222 | (d) usual residential address;
-- src:2223 | (e) the part of the United Kingdom in which the individual is usually resident or, if the individual is usually resident in a country or state outside the United Kingdom, that country or state.
@ref s 167J(1) Required information about a director who is an individual (src:2217-2223)
GIVEN item IS A `s 167J(1) item of information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167J(1) the item is required information about a director who is an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 167J(1) any other information` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The required information about a director (or proposed director) who is an individual is— (a) name, date of birth and nationality; (b) any relevant former names; (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”); (d) usual residential address; (e) the part of the United Kingdom in which the individual is usually resident or, if the individual is usually resident in a country or state outside the United Kingdom, that country or state."
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): a former name is a "relevant former name" unless it falls in an exception: (a) the name known before the adoption of
-- or succession to a title (a peer, or an individual normally known by a British title); (b) in the case of any person,
-- (i) a name changed or disused before the person attained 16, (ii) changed or disused for 20 years or more, (iii) a name
-- the registrar must keep from public inspection or disclosure (regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b)).
-- src:2224 | (2) In subsection (1)(b) “relevant former name” means any former name other than—
-- src:2225 | (a) in the case of a peer, or an individual normally known by a British title, the name by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title, or
-- src:2226 | (b) in the case of any person—
-- src:2227 | (i) a former name which was changed or disused before the person attained the age of 16 years,
-- src:2228 | (ii) a former name which has been changed or disused for 20 years or more, or
-- src:2229 | (iii) a former name which the registrar is required to refrain from making available for public inspection or from disclosing (or both) by virtue of regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b).
@ref s 167J(2) Relevant former name (src:2224-2229)
GIVEN person IS A Individual
      `the name is a former name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a peer, or normally known by a British title, and the name is the one by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the name was changed or disused` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the registrar is required to refrain from making the name available for public inspection or from disclosing it (or both) by virtue of regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167J(2) the name is a relevant former name` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the name is a former name`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant former name” means any former name other than—"
    ELSE IF `the individual is a peer, or normally known by a British title, and the name is the one by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a peer, or an individual normally known by a British title, the name by which the individual was known previous to the adoption of or succession to the title"
         ELSE IF `the day the name was changed or disused` LESS THAN (`add years` (person's `date of birth`) 16)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a former name which was changed or disused before the person attained the age of 16 years"
              ELSE IF `the day in question` AT LEAST (`add years` `the day the name was changed or disused` 20)
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a former name which has been changed or disused for 20 years or more"
                   ELSE IF `the registrar is required to refrain from making the name available for public inspection or from disclosing it (or both) by virtue of regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b)`
                        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a former name which the registrar is required to refrain from making available for public inspection or from disclosing (or both) by virtue of regulations under section 1088(1)(a) or (b)"
                        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2230 | (3) In this section—
-- src:2231 | “former name” means a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes;
-- src:2232 | “name” means the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 167J(3) "former name" and "name" (src:2230-2232)
GIVEN `the name is one by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167J(3) the name is a former name` MEANS
    IF `the name is one by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“former name” means a name by which the individual was formerly known for business purposes"

-- src:2232 | “name” means the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 167J(3) "name" (src:2232)
GIVEN `the item is the individual's forename and surname` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167J(3) the item is the individual's name` MEANS
    IF `the item is the individual's forename and surname`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“name” means the individual’s forename and surname"

-- src:2233 | (4) Where a director (or proposed director) is a peer or an individual usually known by a title, any requirement imposed by this Act to provide the individual’s name because it forms part of the required information may be satisfied by providing that title instead of the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 167J(4) A title may be provided instead of the forename and surname (src:2233)
GIVEN `the director (or proposed director) is a peer or an individual usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the title is provided instead of the individual's forename and surname` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167J(4) the requirement to provide the individual's name is satisfied by providing the title` MEANS
    IF `the director (or proposed director) is a peer or an individual usually known by a title` AND `the title is provided instead of the individual's forename and surname`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a director (or proposed director) is a peer or an individual usually known by a title, any requirement imposed by this Act to provide the individual’s name because it forms part of the required information may be satisfied by providing that title instead"

-- s 167J(5) and (6) (regulations amending the section, affirmative resolution procedure) are machinery: no function.

-- ---- s 167K: required information about a director: corporate directors and firms --------------------------------

DECLARE `s 167K(1) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 167K(1)(a) corporate or firm name`
    `s 167K(1)(b) principal office`
    `s 167K(1)(c) a service address`
    `s 167K(1)(d) the registered number`
    `s 167K(1)(e)(i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed`
    `s 167K(1)(e)(ii) the register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register`
    `s 167K(1) any other information`

-- src:2238 | 167K Required information about a director: corporate directors and firms
-- src:2239 | (1) The required information about a director (or proposed director) that is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, is—
-- src:2240 | (a) corporate or firm name;
-- src:2241 | (b) principal office;
-- src:2242 | (c) a service address (which may be stated as “The company’s registered office”);
-- src:2243 | (d) in the case of a limited company that is a UK-registered company, the registered number;
-- src:2244 | (e) in any other case, particulars of—
-- src:2245 | (i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed, and
-- src:2246 | (ii) if applicable, the register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register.
@ref s 167K(1) Required information about a corporate director or a firm (src:2238-2246)
GIVEN item IS A `s 167K(1) item of information`
      `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate or firm is entered in a register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167K(1) the item is required information about a body corporate or a firm that is a legal person` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 167K(1)(a) corporate or firm name` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 167K(1)(b) principal office` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 167K(1)(c) a service address` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 167K(1)(d) the registered number`
         THEN IF `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` AND `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) in the case of a limited company that is a UK-registered company, the registered number"
    WHEN `s 167K(1)(e)(i) the legal form of the body corporate or firm and the law by which it is governed`
         THEN IF `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` AND `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) in any other case, particulars of"
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 167K(1)(e)(ii) the register in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register`
         THEN IF `s 3(1) the company is a limited company` AND `s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) in any other case, particulars of"
              ELSE IF `the body corporate or firm is entered in a register`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) if applicable, the register in which it is entered"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The required information about a director (or proposed director) that is a body corporate, or a firm that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, is—"

-- s 167K(2) and (3) (regulations amending the section) are machinery: no function.

-- ---- s 167L: directors: offence of failure to notify of changes -----------------------------------------------

-- "fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I": the failure and the lack of excuse are
-- one fact in the text's own words. Whether there was a reasonable excuse is the person's to state (an open-textured
-- judgment the text hands to the court, taken as a plain input by the seat).
-- src:2250 | (1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I, an offence is committed by—
-- src:2251 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 167L(1)(a) Offence by the company (src:2250-2251)
GIVEN `the company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167L(1)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I, an offence is committed by"

-- src:2250 | (1) If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I, an offence is committed by—
-- src:2252 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:2253 | (2) For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 167L(1)(b) and (2) Offence by every officer in default (src:2250 and src:2252-2253)
GIVEN `the company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167L(1)(b) the officer in default commits the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 167G, 167H or 167I, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer"
         OTHERWISE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default`
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; the person is not an officer (the person is an officer of the company)
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is s 1173(1)
    WHERE
        `in default` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"; an officer who is not in default is outside the limit
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121

-- src:2254 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:2255 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:2256 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 167L(3) Penalty for the offence (src:2254-2256)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 167L(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states the penalty only on summary conviction in one of the three places

-- ---- s 167M: prohibition on director acting unless ID verified ---------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "An individual must not act as a director of a company unless the individual's identity is verified". The function says
-- whether the individual contravenes the subsection (JUST TRUE = contravenes).
-- src:2258 | 167M Prohibition on director acting unless ID verified
-- src:2259 | (1) An individual must not act as a director of a company unless the individual’s identity is verified (see section 1110A).
@ref s 167M(1) An individual must not act as a director unless identity verified (src:2258-2259)
GIVEN `the individual acts as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167M(1) the individual contravenes subsection (1) by acting as a director` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the individual acts as a director of the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An individual must not act as a director of a company"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the individual’s identity is verified"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the identity is verified is s 1110A (coa24)

-- (2): "A company must ensure that an individual does not act as a director unless the individual's identity is verified".
-- The duty is stated without a defence: the company contravenes when the individual acts unverified (fork F20).
-- src:2260 | (2) A company must ensure that an individual does not act as a director unless the individual’s identity is verified (see section 1110A).
@ref s 167M(2) A company must ensure that an individual does not act unless identity verified (src:2260)
GIVEN `the individual acts as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167M(2) the company contravenes subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the individual acts as a director of the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must ensure that an individual does not act as a director"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1110A the individual's identity is verified`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the individual’s identity is verified"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the identity is verified is s 1110A (coa24)

-- src:2261 | (3) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence.
@ref s 167M(3) Offence by the individual (src:2261)
GIVEN `the answer under section 167M(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167M(3) the person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 167M(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (1) was contravened is not known

-- src:2262 | (4) If a company contravenes subsection (2) an offence is committed by—
-- src:2263 | (a) the company, and
@ref s 167M(4)(a) Offence by the company (src:2262-2263)
GIVEN `the answer under section 167M(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167M(4)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 167M(2)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company contravenes subsection (2) an offence is committed by"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (2) was contravened is not known

-- src:2262 | (4) If a company contravenes subsection (2) an offence is committed by—
-- src:2264 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:2265 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 167M(4)(b) Offence by every officer in default (src:2262 and src:2264-2265)
GIVEN `the answer under section 167M(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167M(4)(b) the officer in default commits the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 167M(2)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company contravenes subsection (2) an offence is committed by"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the contravention occurred turns on another section's answer
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer"
         OTHERWISE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default`
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; the person is not an officer (the person is an officer of the company)
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is s 1173(1)
    WHERE
        `in default` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"; an officer who is not in default is outside the limit
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121

-- src:2266 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:2267 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:2268 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 167M(5) Penalty for the offence (src:2266-2268)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 167M(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states the penalty only on summary conviction in one of the three places

-- (6): "The only consequences of contravening subsections (1) and (2) are the offences provided for by this section (so that,
-- for example, a contravention does not in any way affect the validity of an individual's acts as a director)."
DECLARE `s 167M(6) consequence of contravening subsection (1) or (2)` IS ONE OF
    `s 167M(6) an offence provided for by section 167M`
    `s 167M(6) the invalidity of the individual's acts as a director`
    `s 167M(6) any other consequence`

-- src:2269 | (6) The only consequences of contravening subsections (1) and (2) are the offences provided for by this section (so that, for example, a contravention does not in any way affect the validity of an individual’s acts as a director).
@ref s 167M(6) The only consequences are the offences (src:2269)
GIVEN consequence IS A `s 167M(6) consequence of contravening subsection (1) or (2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167M(6) the consequence follows from contravening subsection (1) or (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER consequence
    WHEN `s 167M(6) an offence provided for by section 167M` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The only consequences of contravening subsections (1) and (2) are the offences provided for by this section"

-- ---- s 167N: prohibition on acting unless directorship notified -------------------------------------------------

-- (1): the section applies where (a) a person has become a director otherwise than on incorporation and (b) notice under
-- section 167G has not been given within the period in s 167G(6). (2): "The person may not act as a director of the company
-- until notice is given under section 167G": a bar that lifts when notice is given (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on "until").
-- src:2271 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:2272 | (a) a person has become a director of a company otherwise than on its incorporation, and
-- src:2273 | (b) notice under section 167G of the person having done so has not been given within the period mentioned in subsection (6) of that section.
-- src:2274 | (2) The person may not act as a director of the company until notice is given under section 167G.
@ref s 167N(1) and (2) The person may not act as a director until notice is given (src:2271-2274)
GIVEN `the person has become a director of the company otherwise than on its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice under section 167G of the person having done so has not been given within the period mentioned in subsection (6) of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice has now been given under section 167G` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167N(2) the person contravenes subsection (2) by acting as a director` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person has become a director of the company otherwise than on its incorporation` AND `notice under section 167G of the person having done so has not been given within the period mentioned in subsection (6) of that section`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) a person has become a director of a company otherwise than on its incorporation, and (b) notice under section 167G of the person having done so has not been given within the period mentioned in subsection (6) of that section."
    ELSE IF NOT (`the person acts as a director of the company`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person may not act as a director of the company"
         ELSE IF `notice has now been given under section 167G`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until notice is given under section 167G"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2275 | (3) A person who contravenes subsection (2) commits an offence.
@ref s 167N(3) Offence by the person (src:2275)
GIVEN `the answer under section 167N(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167N(3) the person who contravenes subsection (2) commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 167N(2)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who contravenes subsection (2) commits an offence."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (2) was contravened is not known

-- src:2276 | (4) Where the offence is committed by a firm, every officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence.
@ref s 167N(4) Offence by every officer of a firm who is in default (src:2276)
GIVEN `the offence is committed by a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167N(4) the officer in default commits the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offence is committed by a firm`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the offence is committed by a firm, every officer of the firm who is in default also commits the offence."
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `in default`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names officers in default and does not say a shadow director is treated as an officer here (the person is an officer of the firm)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an officer is s 1173(1)
    WHERE
        `in default` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"; an officer who is not in default is outside the limit
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121

-- (5): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under this section to prove that they reasonably believed that
-- notice had been given under section 167G". Where the belief is not proved the answer is JUST FALSE for this provision's
-- defence ("this section gives no defence on these facts"), by the ruling of 2026-11-05 (b).
-- src:2277 | (5) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under this section to prove that they reasonably believed that notice had been given under section 167G.
@ref s 167N(5) Defence (src:2277)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under section 167N` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that they reasonably believed that notice had been given under section 167G` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167N(5) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is charged with an offence under section 167N`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under this section"
    ELSE IF `the person proves that they reasonably believed that notice had been given under section 167G`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to prove that they reasonably believed that notice had been given under section 167G"

-- src:2278 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:2279 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:2280 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 167N(6) Penalty for the offence (src:2278-2280)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 167N(6) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states the penalty only on summary conviction in one of the three places

DECLARE `s 167N(7) consequence of contravening subsection (2)` IS ONE OF
    `s 167N(7) the offence provided for by section 167N`
    `s 167N(7) the invalidity of the person's acts as a director`
    `s 167N(7) any other consequence`

-- src:2281 | (7) The only consequence of a contravention of subsection (2) is the offence provided for by this section (so that, for example, a contravention does not in any way affect the validity of a person’s acts as a director).
@ref s 167N(7) The only consequence is the offence (src:2281)
GIVEN consequence IS A `s 167N(7) consequence of contravening subsection (2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 167N(7) the consequence follows from contravening subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER consequence
    WHEN `s 167N(7) the offence provided for by section 167N` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The only consequence of a contravention of subsection (2) is the offence provided for by this section"
